    "emitted_by": "the node exporter with the restricted collectors, scraped as the node_exporter job on 127.0.0.1:9100",
    "metrics": ["node_vmstat_oom_kill", "node_filesystem_avail_bytes", "node_filesystem_size_bytes", "node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes", "node_load1"]
  },
  "polaris": {
    "emitted_by": "Polaris 1.8.0 (Quarkus 3.39.3, Micrometer 1.17.1 with the Prometheus simpleclient registry) on its management port, scraped as the polaris job. Names and labels read from the pinned sources: the HTTP server timer http.server.requests (the quarkus-micrometer HTTP server binder: the timer carries method, uri, outcome and status only, and the active requests gauge carries server.port and url.scheme), the active requests gauge, the JVM memory binder (JvmMemoryMetrics, tags area and id) and the common tag application from polaris.metrics.tags in the runtime defaults. Polaris publishes the timer buckets only when polaris.metrics.http-server-requests.histogram-slos is set (MetricsConfiguration, MeterFilterProducer), so the task sets POLARIS_METRICS_HTTP_SERVER_REQUESTS_HISTOGRAM_SLOS to 10ms,50ms,100ms,500ms,1s,5s (Quarkus DurationConverter reads the ms and s units) and the series has the le values 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.5, 1.0, 5.0 and +Inf. Non-application paths such as /q are not counted, and Quarkus allows 100 uri values at most.",
    "metrics": {
      "http_server_requests_seconds_count": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["method", "uri", "outcome", "status", "application"]},
      "http_server_requests_seconds_sum": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["method", "uri", "outcome", "status", "application"]},
      "http_server_requests_seconds_bucket": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["method", "uri", "outcome", "status", "application", "le"]},
      "http_server_requests_seconds_max": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["method", "uri", "outcome", "status", "application"]},
      "http_server_active_requests": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["server_port", "url_scheme", "application"]},
      "jvm_memory_used_bytes": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["area", "id", "application"]},
      "jvm_memory_committed_bytes": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["area", "id", "application"]},
      "jvm_memory_max_bytes": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["area", "id", "application"]}
    }
  },
  "mlflow": {
    "emitted_by": "MLflow 3.17.2 with prometheus-flask-exporter 0.23.2 and prometheus-client 0.26.0, started with --expose-prometheus and read through the relay of the host state exporter, scraped as the mlflow job. Names and labels read from the pinned sources: mlflow/server/prometheus_exporter.py sets the prefix mlflow, excludes /health and /version and groups the latency by a function named mlflow_version, so the latency has the labels method, mlflow_version and status and no route or endpoint label. The latency uses the prometheus-client default buckets. The metrics endpoint is not counted. Only the Flask routes (the tracking and registry REST calls) are counted.",
    "metrics": {
      "mlflow_http_request_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["method", "status"]},
      "mlflow_http_request_exceptions_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["method", "status"]},
      "mlflow_http_request_duration_seconds": {"type": "histogram", "labels": ["method", "mlflow_version", "status"]}
    }
  },
  "grafana": {
    "emitted_by": "Grafana 13.2.5 on its HTTP port, scraped as the grafana job. Names and labels read from the v13.2.5 source: pkg/services/ngalert/metrics (scheduler.go, multi_org_alertmanager.go) for the alerting series and pkg/infra/httpclient/httpclientprovider/datasource_metrics_middleware.go for the data source series. The notification counters skip zero values (WithSkipZeroValueMetrics), so a series is absent until its first notification and its first sample is already one: increase and rate cannot see that first step, and the entries say starts_at_first_event. process_start_time_seconds comes from the client_golang process collector, which Grafana's /metrics handler serves through prometheus.DefaultGatherer (pkg/infra/metrics/service.go, pkg/api/http_server.go); it is the Unix time of the process start, so it changes at a restart.",
    "metrics": {
      "grafana_alerting_rule_evaluations_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["org"]},
      "grafana_alerting_rule_evaluation_failures_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["org"]},
      "grafana_alerting_rule_evaluation_duration_seconds": {"type": "histogram", "labels": ["org"]},
      "grafana_alerting_scheduler_behind_seconds": {"type": "gauge", "labels": []},
      "grafana_alerting_schedule_alert_rules": {"type": "gauge", "labels": []},
      "grafana_alerting_rule_groups": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["org"]},
      "grafana_alerting_schedule_rule_evaluations_missed_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["org", "name", "reason"]},
      "grafana_alerting_alertmanager_alerts": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["org", "state"]},
      "grafana_alerting_notifications_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["org", "integration"], "starts_at_first_event": true},
      "grafana_alerting_notifications_failed_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["org", "integration"], "starts_at_first_event": true},
      "grafana_alerting_notification_latency_seconds": {"type": "histogram", "labels": []},
      "grafana_datasource_request_total": {"type": "counter", "labels": ["datasource", "datasource_type", "code", "method", "secure_socks_ds_proxy_enabled"]},
      "grafana_datasource_request_duration_seconds": {"type": "histogram", "labels": ["datasource", "datasource_type", "code", "method", "secure_socks_ds_proxy_enabled"]},
      "process_start_time_seconds": {"type": "gauge", "labels": []},
      "grafana_datasource_request_in_flight": {"type": "gauge", "labels": ["datasource", "datasource_type", "secure_socks_ds_proxy_enabled"]}
    }
  }
}
